    "https://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204592": {
      "title": "Lecturer of Counselor Education",
      "description": "SUNY Oneonta\nJob Posting: Lecturer of Counselor Education SUNY Oneonta \n\tJob Posting: Lecturer of Counselor Education Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Lecturer of Counselor Education Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Educational Psychology, Counseling and Special Education Locations: Oneonta, NY Posted: Sep 9, 2026 Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $50,063.00 - $55,000.00 Position ID: 204592 Share Job Description: Help prepare the next generation of professional school counselors as a Lecturer of Counselor Education within our Master of Science in Education School Counseling Program. This is an exciting opportunity for a dedicated counselor educator to teach graduate-level courses, supervise practicum and internship experiences, and contribute to the success of a supportive, student-centered program. This is a full-time, 10-month academic appointment. The Lecturer will report to the Chair of the Department of Educational Psychology, Counseling and Special Education and will play an integral role in the delivery of our CACREP-aligned School Counseling curriculum. The goal of our School Counseling Program is to prepare counselors to work in school settings using comprehensive developmental programs based on the American School Counselor Association (ASCA) National Model. Faculty and candidates work closely together in small cohorts, fostering a collegial and hands-on learning environment. Our graduates serve as school counselors throughout New York State and beyond, and our program maintains strong partnerships with local school districts that provide rich field-based training opportunities. Faculty regularly collaborate across departments and engage in activities related to ASCA and CACREP standards, school counselor preparation, and clinical supervision. To learn more about our university and the department, please visit https://suny.oneonta.edu/ and https://suny.oneonta.edu/educational-psychology-counseling-and-special-education . Duties include but are not limited to: Teaching graduate-level courses within the School Counseling program. Supervising students in practicum and internship placements. Participating in curriculum development, program assessment, and continuous improvement efforts aligned with ASCA and CACREP standards. Engaging in departmental, college, and university service activities. Maintaining active involvement in the school counseling profession. Salary: $50,063 - $55,000 commensurate with experience. SUNY Oneonta is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness qualifying employer. Information on SUNY's comprehensive benefits offerings can be found at https://www.suny.edu/benefits . Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Requirements: Required Qualifications: Master's degree in School Counseling from a regionally accredited college or university. Professional experience in counseling, counselor education, or a related field. Preferred: Ph.D. in Counselor Education and Supervision or a closely related field from a regionally accredited college or university. Certification and/or licensure appropriate to School Counseling. A minimum of four years of professional school counseling experience. Experience teaching one or more of the following courses: Counseling Techniques, Group Counseling, School Counseling Practicum, and/or School Counseling Internship. Knowledge of ASCA (American School Counselor Association) National Model standards. Knowledge of CACREP (Council for Accreditation of Counseling and Related Educational Programs) standards. Training and/or experience providing clinical supervision. Experience working with diverse and/or multicultural populations through teaching, mentoring, research, service, or professional practice. Additional Information: SUNY Oneonta enrolls about 5,500 students who pursue bachelor's or master's degrees or certificates in one of 70-plus academic programs. Known as an exemplary residential campus that values inclusion, service and sustainability, SUNY Oneonta is a nurturing community where students grow intellectually, thrive socially, and live purposefully. The university is located in the City of Oneonta, nestled in the northern foothills of the Catskill Mountains about a four-hour drive from New York City, Boston, and Philadelphia. With a population just shy of 14,000, Oneonta is one of the 20 Most Picturesque Small Towns in America, according to Microsoft News. The natural beauty of the region is breathtaking year-round. Each season offers outdoor activities such as hiking, biking, boating, swimming, and skiing. Employees give SUNY Oneonta high marks for work/life balance, management, and culture. The university's indeed.com rating is 4.4, with one recent review noting that the people are what make SUNY Oneonta so special. SUNY Oneonta values a diverse university community. Please visit our website on diversity at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/diversity . Moreover, the university is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Women, persons of color, persons with disabilities, and protected veterans are encouraged to apply. \"At SUNY Oneonta, we believe that diversity is an asset and a source of strength that energizes our collective growth and innovation.\" - President Alberto Cardelle. Application Instructions: To apply online go to: http://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/candapply.jsp?JOBID=204592 . Please upload a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, copies of any relevant school counseling certifications and/or licenses, and unofficial transcripts. Contact information for three references must be provided; instructions for submitting letters of reference will be sent directly to the referees. For other employment and regional opportunities, please visit our website at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/about-oneonta/employment . Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Oneonta 108 Ravine Parkway, Oneonta, NY 13820"
    },
    "https://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204754": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Operations for the Extended and Community Learning (ExCL) Center",
      "description": "SUNY Oneonta\nJob Posting: Associate Director of Operations for the Extended and Community Learning (ExCL) Center SUNY Oneonta \n\tJob Posting: Associate Director of Operations for the Extended and Community Learning (ExCL) Center Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Associate Director of Operations for the Extended and Community Learning (ExCL) Center Category: Professional Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Department of Extended and Community Learning Locations: Oneonta, NY Posted: Sep 11, 2026 Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $72,000.00 - $72,000.00 Position ID: 204754 Share Job Description: The Associate Director of Operations for the Extended and Community Learning (ExCL) Center is responsible for overseeing the daily operations of the Center and providing administrative leadership for a wide range of complex functions. These include enrollment management, registration processes, non-degree admissions, program management, community and extended learning initiatives, and student support services. Reporting to the Director, the Associate Director ensures the effective delivery of programs, services, and operations for non-degree learners, College in High School programing, visiting students, auditors, while maintaining compliance with institutional and accreditation standards. The Associate Director collaborates with Deans, faculty, academic departments, campus community partners, and delivers high-level student and family support, supervises staff, and represents the Center as the Director's designee when needed. To learn more about the University and the department, please visit https://suny.oneonta.edu/ or https://suny.oneonta.edu/academics/extended-learning . Duties may include: Overseeing student enrollment, registration, and student management operations for the ExCL Center, including: Student information and student management systems, including SLATE, BANNER, and Non-Credit Student Management Systems Non-degree admission processes in SLATE, including application review, data entry, and decision processing in BANNER Application processing, registration activities, and payment procedures Course section creation and related enrollment activities in BANNER Management of enrollment for course auditors Management of day-to-day operations for College in High School Dual Enrollment programming Analysis of business processes and recommendation of technology-driven efficiencies Collaboration with campus departments and partners to align system functionality with business needs Oversight of the creation, maintenance, and continuous improvement of functional documentation, procedures, and workflows Serving as the primary advisor for non-degree students, providing guidance and support through orientation, academic progress monitoring, retention efforts, and delivery of high-quality customer service to students, families, and community participants Administering the Cross-Registration process for visiting students Assisting in the development and oversight of Winter and Summer Intersession set-up and enrollment processes Supporting the SUNY Oneonta Migrant Leadership Academy (SOMLA), Access and Opportunity Program (AOP) Summer Academy, and other similar programs through course development, admissions, and enrollment Developing and maintain strong relationships with high school administrators, instructors, University Deans, faculty, academic leadership, applicants, and other College in High School partners; serve as the primary point of contact for Dual Enrollment programming and manage communications with applicants Ensuring compliance with university policies, accreditation standards, and NYS Department of Education Dual Enrollment Agreement requirements, including maintaining accurate and up-to-date MOUs with high school partners, maintaining accurate records, safeguarding data integrity, and ensuring timely deposits and proper financial tracking of program revenue for College in High School programming Collaborating closely with the Director to support the development, implementation, administration, and continuous improvement of new and emerging ExCL programs, strategic initiatives, and operational priorities Supervising one Office Assistant and provide operational leadership, guidance, training, mentoring, project oversight, work coordination, and support for office operations Collaborating with the Marketing and Communications Office to ensure website accuracy Contributing to budget planning, monitoring, and oversight of program funds, and track, analyze, and report on program performance to support continuous improvement Providing office coverage as needed, respond to inquiries via phone, email, and in person Representing the ExCL Center as the Director's designee when needed Salary: $72,000. SUNY Oneonta is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness qualifying employer. Information on SUNY's comprehensive benefits offerings can be found at https://www.suny.edu/benefits/ Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Requirements: Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree required Minimum 3-5 years of experience in higher education administration, admissions, enrollment management, registrar operations, or continuing education administration. Experience with student management systems and operations, student services, program coordination, and supervision Minimum 3-5 years of experience with Banner in a professional environment Working knowledge of FERPA and academic records compliance Knowledge of cash handling procedures, compliance, and enrollment management practices Additional: Ability to manage multiple programs, deadlines, and responsibilities simultaneously Strong analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills Strong operations management background Preferred: Experience processing student and course data submissions Demonstrated Banner experience across multiple modules (e.g, Student Registration), with the ability to troubleshoot and implement systems changes Experience with system implementations, upgrades, and functional testing Experience working with and serving diverse populations Additional Information: SUNY Oneonta enrolls about 5,500 students who pursue bachelor's or master's degrees or certificates in one of 70-plus academic programs. Known as an exemplary residential campus that values inclusion, service and sustainability, SUNY Oneonta is a nurturing community where students grow intellectually, thrive socially, and live purposefully. The university is located in the City of Oneonta, nestled in the northern foothills of the Catskill Mountains about a four-hour drive from New York City, Boston, and Philadelphia. With a population just shy of 14,000, Oneonta is one of the 20 Most Picturesque Small Towns in America, according to Microsoft News. The natural beauty of the region is breathtaking year-round. Each season offers outdoor activities such as hiking, biking, boating, swimming, and skiing. Employees give SUNY Oneonta high marks for work/life balance, management, and culture. The university's indeed.com rating is 4.4, with one recent review noting that the people are what make SUNY Oneonta so special. SUNY Oneonta values a diverse university community. Please visit our website on diversity at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/about/mission-values-vision/inclusivity Moreover, the university is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Women, persons of color, persons with disabilities, and protected veterans are encouraged to apply. \"At SUNY Oneonta, we believe that diversity is an asset and a source of strength that energizes our collective growth and innovation.\" - President Alberto Cardelle. Application Instructions: To apply online go to: [Employment opportunities will add] Please upload a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references (required). For other employment and regional opportunities, please visit our website at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/about-oneonta/employment. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Oneonta 108 Ravine Parkway, Oneonta, NY 13820"
    },
    "https://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204789": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Housing and Data",
      "description": "SUNY Oneonta\nJob Posting: Assistant Director of Housing and Data SUNY Oneonta \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Director of Housing and Data Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Director of Housing and Data Category: Professional Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Residential Experience and Housing Locations: Oneonta, NY Posted: Sep 14, 2026 Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $57,151.00 - $62,000.00 Position ID: 204789 Share Job Description: SUNY Oneonta is seeking a community development focused leader to join our team as Assistant Director of Housing and Data . The Assistant Director reports directly to the Director of Residence Life and Housing and functions under a flexible work schedule that may include weekend and evening hours. Residence Life and Housing fosters an inclusive environment for growth and learning; provides high-quality facilities, services, and programs; and supports student academic success and retention. Our goals are to build a residential program that fosters a spirit of engagement and community among students, staff, and faculty, to foster a sense of belonging to the residential community through student engagement and leadership in governance, and to promote student academic success. The Office of On Campus Housing and Residence Life is under the Residential Experience and Housing Department, which also houses offices of Move-In, Orientation and Welcome; as well as the Office of Off Campus and Commuter Students. Our office works closely with many other areas of the University through committee work, collaboration, and resource sharing. To learn more about the University and the department, please visit https://suny.oneonta.edu/ or https://suny.oneonta.edu/residential-experience-and-housing . Duties may include: Supervision of 4-6 Residence Hall Directors. Oversight of the occupancy program for 3,000 bed campus. Design and execution of new and returning housing application and assignment processes. Management of room changes. Administration of residential damage billing process. Assistance with furniture procurement and renovation planning. Maintenance and administration of the housing database StarRez. Assistance with card access system. Design and distribution of weekly reports for the department, division, and university stakeholders. Assistance in compiling and analyzing historic and current occupancy data to inform occupancy projections. Serving as department liaison with Student Accounts and Dining Services as it relates to student bills. Participation in on call duty rotation. Assistance with emergency/crisis management for the department. Chairing department committees. Salary: $57,151- $62,000 commensurate with experience. SUNY Oneonta is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) qualifying employer. Information on SUNY's comprehensive benefits offerings can be found at https://www.suny.edu/benefits . Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree. One (1) year or more experience supervising, evaluating, and selecting staff. Experience managing building occupancy. Experience with emergencies or crisis response (duty rotation). Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Experience with excel spreadsheets or other data management systems. Preferred: Master's degree in Higher Education Administration or related field. Experience with StarRez or similar occupancy database systems. Experience with card access management systems. Experience working with housing accommodations. Ability to work effectively under pressure and meet established goals and objectives. Ability to work independently and take initiative on projects. Experience working with and serving diverse populations. Additional Information: SUNY Oneonta enrolls about 5,500 students who pursue bachelor's or master's degrees or certificates in one of 70-plus academic programs. Known as an exemplary residential campus that values inclusion, service and sustainability, SUNY Oneonta is a nurturing community where students grow intellectually, thrive socially, and live purposefully. The university is located in the City of Oneonta, nestled in the northern foothills of the Catskill Mountains about a four-hour drive from New York City, Boston, and Philadelphia. With a population just shy of 14,000, Oneonta is one of the 20 Most Picturesque Small Towns in America, according to Microsoft News. The natural beauty of the region is breathtaking year-round. Each season offers outdoor activities such as hiking, biking, boating, swimming, and skiing. Employees give SUNY Oneonta high marks for work/life balance, management, and culture. The university's indeed.com rating is 4.4, with one recent review noting that the people are what make SUNY Oneonta so special. SUNY Oneonta values a diverse university community. Please visit our website on diversity at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/about/mission-values-vision/inclusivity . Moreover, the University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Women, persons of color, persons with disabilities, and protected veterans are encouraged to apply. \"At SUNY Oneonta, we believe that diversity is an asset and a source of strength that energizes our collective growth and innovation.\" - President Alberto Cardelle. Application Instructions: To apply online go to: http://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/candapply.jsp?JOBID=204789 . Please upload a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references (required). For other employment and regional opportunities, please visit our website at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/about-oneonta/employment . Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Oneonta 108 Ravine Parkway, Oneonta, NY 13820"
    },
    "https://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204813": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Director for Employee Services",
      "description": "SUNY Oneonta\nJob Posting: Assistant/Associate Director for Employee Services SUNY Oneonta \n\tJob Posting: Assistant/Associate Director for Employee Services Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant/Associate Director for Employee Services Category: Management / Confidential Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Employee Services Locations: Oneonta, NY Posted: Sep 15, 2026 Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $90,000.00 - $95,000.00 Position ID: 204813 Share Job Description: People are at the heart of everything we do. As Assistant/Associate Director of Employee Services , you'll help employees, supervisors, and campus leaders navigate complex workplace situations, strengthen working relationships, and support a positive and productive university community. Working closely with the Chief Human Resources Officer (CHRO), you'll have the opportunity to lead or provide guidance on employee and labor relations matters, payroll and benefits administration, performance management, workplace conflict resolution, training and development, and compliance. Employee Services at SUNY Oneonta is dedicated to supporting the growth and success of every member of our campus community. Through partnership, problem-solving, and responsive service, the department strives to offer an exceptional employee experience while supporting individual success and advancing the University's mission. To learn more about the University and the department, please visit https://suny.oneonta.edu/ or https://suny.oneonta.edu/about/university-offices/employee-services . Duties May Include: Provide leadership, supervision, mentoring, and performance management for assigned Employee Services team members. Establish priorities, coordinate workflows, and support the effective delivery of various employee related services. Contribute to departmental projects, initiatives, and continuous improvement efforts. Conduct workplace investigations and support disciplinary processes in accordance with established policies, procedures, and applicable collective bargaining agreements. Provide consultation and guidance to supervisors and employees on a wide range of employee relations matters such as performance management, workplace concerns and policy interpretation. Resolve workplace conflicts by facilitating discussions, recommending solutions, and ensuring issues are handled with fairness and confidentiality. Develop and deliver training in partnership with the CHRO on leadership, employee relations, performance management, workplace expectations, and policy and regulatory compliance. Build and guide processes for employment-related functions such as benefits, payroll, and recruitment administration. Exercise exceptional judgment and uphold the highest standards of ethics, professionalism, discretion, and confidentiality when handling sensitive and complex matters. Salary: $90,000 - $95,000 commensurate with experience. SUNY Oneonta is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) qualifying employer. Information on SUNY's comprehensive benefits offerings can be found at https://www.suny.edu/benefits . Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree from a regionally accredited institution. Minimum of 6 years' progressive Human Resources experience, with at least 4 years' HR experience at the mid/high management level, leading, supervising, or coordinating the work of other human resources staff members. Demonstrated experience conducting workplace investigations. Highly effective written and oral communication skills. Impeccable confidentiality and ethical standards. Additional : Strong knowledge of HR best practices, employment law, and compliance requirements. Evidence of outstanding cultural competency and working successfully with employees from varied backgrounds in the workplace. Deep experience with employee relations and sensitive workplace matters. Extensive knowledge of, and ability to understand and apply employment laws, regulations, policies, and collective bargaining agreements. Preferred: Current PHR/SPHR, SHRM-CP/SHRM-SCP, or similar HR certification. Master's degree in human resources, business administration, social sciences, labor relations, public administration, or other related discipline. Experience supporting payroll and/or benefits administration. Experience developing and delivering employee related training programs. Additional Information: SUNY Oneonta enrolls about 5,500 students who pursue bachelor's or master's degrees or certificates in one of 70-plus academic programs. Known as an exemplary residential campus that values inclusion, service and sustainability, SUNY Oneonta is a nurturing community where students grow intellectually, thrive socially, and live purposefully. The university is located in the City of Oneonta, nestled in the northern foothills of the Catskill Mountains about a four-hour drive from New York City, Boston, and Philadelphia. With a population just shy of 14,000, Oneonta is one of the 20 Most Picturesque Small Towns in America, according to Microsoft News. The natural beauty of the region is breathtaking year-round. Each season offers outdoor activities such as hiking, biking, boating, swimming, and skiing. Employees give SUNY Oneonta high marks for work/life balance, management, and culture. The university's indeed.com rating is 4.4, with one recent review noting that the people are what make SUNY Oneonta so special. SUNY Oneonta values a diverse university community. Please visit our website on diversity at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/diversity . Moreover, the University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Women, persons of color, persons with disabilities, and protected veterans are encouraged to apply. \"At SUNY Oneonta, we believe that diversity is an asset and a source of strength that energizes our collective growth and innovation.\" - President Alberto Cardelle. Application Instructions: To apply online go to: http://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/candapply.jsp?JOBID=204813 . Please upload a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references (required). For full consideration, applications should be submitted by September 25, 2026 . For other employment and regional opportunities, please visit our website at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/about-oneonta/employment . Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Oneonta 108 Ravine Parkway, Oneonta, NY 13820"
    },
    "https://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205231": {
      "title": "Workforce Development Coordinator",
      "description": "SUNY Oneonta\nJob Posting: Workforce Development Coordinator SUNY Oneonta \n\tJob Posting: Workforce Development Coordinator Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Workforce Development Coordinator Category: Professional Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Extended and Community Learning (ExCL) Center Locations: Oneonta, NY Posted: Sep 25, 2026 Type: Full-time Temporary Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $57,151.00 - $57,151.00 Position ID: 205231 Share Job Description: The Workforce Development Coordinator serves as a key member of the Extended and Community Learning (ExCL) Center team and is responsible for the planning, coordination, implementation, administration, and continuous improvement of workforce development and continuing education initiatives that support regional economic development and lifelong learning. This position serves as an ambassador for SUNY Oneonta and the ExCL Center by fostering strategic partnerships that advance workforce development, career readiness, adult education, and economic mobility throughout the region. To learn more about the University and the department, please visit https://suny.oneonta.edu/ or https://suny.oneonta.edu/academics/extended-learning . Duties May Include: Developing, implementing, administering, and evaluating workforce development, continuing education, professional development, apprenticeship, certificate, customized training, and grant-funded programs that support the mission of the ExCL Center and SUNY Oneonta. Building and maintaining collaborative relationships with employers, workforce development agencies, government organizations, educational institutions, workforce investment partners, economic development organizations, and community stakeholders to identify workforce needs, develop responsive training solutions, and expand educational opportunities throughout the region. Coordinating all aspects of workforce programming, including program logistics, scheduling, facilities, technology, registration, instructional materials, purchasing, contracts, learner support services, and the recruitment and support of instructors, subject matter experts, and training partners. Managing multiple projects simultaneously while monitoring program quality, participant outcomes, timelines, deliverables, compliance requirements, and performance metrics; collecting and reporting data and recommending improvements to enhance program effectiveness and operational efficiency. Providing exceptional customer service and learner support throughout recruitment, enrollment, training participation, program completion, and credential attainment while utilizing student information systems, customer relationship management platforms, learning management systems, and other enterprise technologies to support program operations. Conducting outreach, researching workforce and labor market trends, and representing the ExCL Center and SUNY Oneonta at employer visits, workforce summits, career fairs, conferences, advisory boards, community meetings, networking events, and other activities that advance workforce development initiatives and institutional priorities. Performing work in a dynamic environment requiring independent judgment, collaboration with internal and external stakeholders, occasional evening and weekend hours, local travel, and attendance at off-site meetings and events. Salary: $57,151. SUNY Oneonta is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) qualifying employer. Information on SUNY's comprehensive benefits offerings can be found at https://www.suny.edu/benefits . Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree. Minimum of three (3) years of experience in program management, workforce development, community engagement, nonprofit administration, training coordination, or a closely related field. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple programs, projects, deadlines, and competing priorities simultaneously. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications and other technology platforms used to support program administration and operations. Ability to work occasional evenings and weekends as needed. Valid driver's license at time of appointment. Preferred: Experience working in workforce development, economic development, adult education, or a related field. Experience developing, implementing, administering, and evaluating educational, workforce development, training, or grant-funded programs. Experience building partnerships with employers, workforce agencies, community organizations, educational institutions, and other external stakeholders. Experience using student information systems, customer relationship management (CRM) platforms, registration systems, learning management systems, or similar technologies (e.g., Banner, Slate, Salesforce). Knowledge of workforce development practices, labor market trends, adult learning principles, enrollment management, and regional workforce needs. Experience working with and serving diverse populations. Additional Information: To apply online go to: http://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/candapply.jsp?JOBID=205231 . Please upload a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references (required). For other employment and regional opportunities, please visit our website at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/about-oneonta/employment . Application Instructions: SUNY Oneonta enrolls about 5,500 students who pursue bachelor's or master's degrees or certificates in one of 70-plus academic programs. Known as an exemplary residential campus that values inclusion, service and sustainability, SUNY Oneonta is a nurturing community where students grow intellectually, thrive socially, and live purposefully. The university is located in the City of Oneonta, nestled in the northern foothills of the Catskill Mountains about a four-hour drive from New York City, Boston, and Philadelphia. With a population just shy of 14,000, Oneonta is one of the 20 Most Picturesque Small Towns in America, according to Microsoft News. The natural beauty of the region is breathtaking year-round. Each season offers outdoor activities such as hiking, biking, boating, swimming, and skiing. Employees give SUNY Oneonta high marks for work/life balance, management, and culture. The university's indeed.com rating is 4.4, with one recent review noting that the people are what make SUNY Oneonta so special. SUNY Oneonta values a diverse university community. Please visit our website on diversity at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/diversity . Moreover, the University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Women, persons of color, persons with disabilities, and protected veterans are encouraged to apply. \"At SUNY Oneonta, we believe that diversity is an asset and a source of strength that energizes our collective growth and innovation.\" - President Alberto Cardelle. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Oneonta 108 Ravine Parkway, Oneonta, NY 13820"
